      "description": "Smoky Mountain Holdings LLC is the manager-level joint venture owning four operating hydroelectric facilities in eastern Tennessee and western North Carolina: Cheoah, Calderwood, Chilhowee and Santeetlah. The portfolio totals 377 MW and has produced approximately 1.4 million MWh in an average year. Brookfield acquired the former Alcoa Tapoco assets in 2012. Argo Infrastructure Partners affiliate AMF Kimble Holdings acquired 50% in March 2023, while Brookfield affiliates and institutional partners retained the other 50%. TVA signed a 10-year power purchase agreement beginning in 2025, and the company closed a $435 million financing in August 2025. Brookfield Infrastructure Income Fund separately reports exposure beginning in March 2023; it was not the original 2012 acquisition vehicle. No later platform sale, signed pending exit or ownership transfer was identified through August 16, 2026. The four dams are underlying assets and are not separate portfolio companies.",
